</ix:nonNumeric><p id="xdx_8A5_zAnE1Mw9rQsk" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
of March 31, 2025 and September 30, 2025, the allowance for credit losses amounted to RMB<span id="xdx_901_eus-gaap--AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivableCurrent_iI_pn5n6_c20250331_zQ9jN8bnGp2e" title="Allowance for credit losses"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivableCurrent" contextRef="AsOf2025-03-31" id="Fact001226" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-5" scale="6" unitRef="RMB">52.8</ix:nonFraction></span>
million and RMB<span id="xdx_90C_eus-gaap--AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivableCurrent_iI_pn5n6_c20250930_z2DHRBlhCnP3" title="Allowance for credit losses"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:AllowanceForDoubtfulAccountsReceivableCurrent" contextRef="AsOf2025-09-30" id="Fact001228" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-5" scale="6" unitRef="RMB">46.1</ix:nonFraction></span>
million, respectively. The Company determined that the collection of these customers&#8217; receivable is not probable due to
financial difficulties experienced by related customers.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>




